00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:32.050
and the answer here is sorry okay anyway
okay so what makes weather hard to

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:39.310
predict and the answer is chaos so what
is chaos I mean we all use the word

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:45.610
chaos colloquially sometimes we'll talk
about chaotic systems and systems being

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:50.530
hard to protect but from a mathematical
perspective when I say something's

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:55.840
chaotic or when other mathematicians say
this we mean something very specific

00:14:55.840 --> 00:15:01.950
so chaos the features of tasks the most
important feature is this idea of

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:07.660
sensitivity to initial conditions you've
probably heard of the butterfly effect

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:14.140
so colloquially the butterfly effect is
the butterfly flaps its wings in let's

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:20.710
say South Africa then maybe that
influences a hurricane happening in the

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:26.050
Caribbean now when when I think about
the butterfly effect I really think

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:32.110
about it as the difference between two
nearby initial conditions one where the

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:36.100
butterfly doesn't flap his wings at that
instant in time and one where the

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:41.830
butterfly does laughs its wings and the
small change in initial conditions can

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:47.260
lead to a very different weather
trajectory down the line because weather

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:54.820
is a chaotic system and so here this is
an example an illustration of what we

00:15:54.820 --> 00:16:01.839
call a chaotic billiard so we have these
two billiard balls in red and in yellow

00:16:01.839 --> 00:16:07.150
and they're having some trajectories
starting very close by to each other but

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:12.580
not at the exact same point but both
under this blue star somewhere and I'm

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:17.550
gonna plot the trajectory of one of them
in yellow and the other in red and

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:23.160
I look as they bounce off this surface
the distance between the trajectories

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:31.350
grows in time and in fact that distance
grows exponentially so this is the

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:35.190
technical part that I'm going to come
back to later on so this is a technical

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:40.040
heart that I want you to get out of this
talk is this notion of a Liana of time

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:45.600
so that's the time over which this
distance between these two things that

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:51.720
started out really close together the
time over which that distance increases

00:16:51.720 --> 00:17:03.240
by a factor of e Euler's number which is
2.71828 etc now in into Li up and half

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:08.610
times that distance increases by a
factor a squared + 3 Li up and off times

00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:16.110
e cubed etc all right in this system
because this difference is increasing

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:20.970
exponentially long term prediction is
impossible you have to specify the

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:27.000
initial conditions precisely if you want
to predict in the long term but in the

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:33.870
medium term you can hope to make some
decent predictions also in the medium

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:37.890
term and in the long term the behavior
of these kinds of systems can appear

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:42.300
random in fact these even though the
system is completely deterministic the

00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:47.090
physics is completely known we know how
it bounces off these surfaces where each

00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:54.090
billiard is going to go but in the long
run it looks random fact chaotic systems

00:17:54.090 --> 00:18:00.059
like this are used for random number
generation or can be used so that's one

00:18:00.059 --> 00:18:04.919
kind of system that's hard to predict
another kind of system that's hard to

00:18:04.919 --> 00:18:09.870
predict is one that is not deterministic
like we know all the physics and we know

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:15.330
if we could specify this exactly we
would know what happens next and these

00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:18.870
other kinds of systems the systems with
randomness are ones that we call

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:23.929
stochastic systems and they can also be
hard to predict often having a lot of

00:18:23.929 --> 00:18:28.840
independent actors so for example as in
the stock

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:34.169
market there are trends there definite
patterns in the stock market but

00:18:34.169 --> 00:18:39.840
prediction over the medium term long
term virtually impossible other systems

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:45.669
where this happens you can look at the
behavior of many interacting agents have

00:18:45.669 --> 00:18:54.159
these features of stochasticity so how
can machine learning help us predict the

00:18:54.159 --> 00:18:58.600
unpredictable so there have been a
variety of different methods for

